# Shipped class-cast library for the conversion editor.
# Each 'cast <Name> ... end' block defines a class-to-class cast the DSL names as the
# '#link To <- From : <Name>' suffix. The editor uses name/accepts/yields.
#
# The realization hints (dfm/compat/pas/todo) are EDITOR-SIDE ONLY as of 2026-09-04.
# This header used to say the engine's convert-apply consumes them. It does not, and
# never has -- nothing under srceport\ or src\cli\ reads a .castlib. Spec item G6.3
# asked for the comment to be corrected or the consumer built; the comment is now
# correct and building the consumer remains open work.
#
# Since 2026-09-04 the engine DOES split the ': <Name>' suffix off the #link FromPath
# (it used to swallow it and then report the valid line as a missing path), and
# convert-apply refuses to rewrite a .pas access site for a link carrying a cast
# rather than renaming without performing the conversion.
# Strict 7-bit ASCII, CRLF.

cast AssignGraphic
  accepts TPicture, TBitmap, TGraphic, TPngImage, TIcon
  yields  TdxSmartGlyph
  dfm     keep-bytes-if-compatible
  compat  png, bmp
  pas     '{dst}.Assign({src});'
  todo    'transfer image from {src} by hand (TBitmap/TPicture -> TdxSmartGlyph)'
end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ENUM casts. Named by the same '#link To <- From : <Name>' suffix as a class
# cast, and EXECUTED by the engine: convert-apply/convert-reemit translate the
# .dfm value member by member when the rule book names the cast and the run is
# given --castlib.
#
# Grammar, chosen to mirror the two DSLs it sits between so there is nothing new
# to learn: 'from'/'to' match '#mapping <Name> from <T> to <T>', the '->' in a
# 'map' line matches a '#when ... -> ...' branch, and 'else' matches '#else'.
# One pair per line, so the file stays diffable and a tool can append a line
# without rewriting one.
#
# MATCHING IS BY NAME, NOT ORDINAL. Two enums being converted are different
# types whose members correspond by MEANING; equal ordinals across unrelated
# types are a coincidence, not evidence.
#
# Without an 'else', a value no 'map' line covers is NOT written and is reported
# as `enum-cast-unmapped`. That is deliberate: the target is a different enum
# type, so passing the source member name through either fails to load or
# quietly means something else.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

enum ButtonLayout
  from Vcl.Buttons.TButtonLayout
  to   dxCore.TdxButtonLayout
  map  blGlyphLeft -> dxblGlyphLeft
  map  blGlyphRight -> dxblGlyphRight
  map  blGlyphTop -> dxblGlyphTop
  map  blGlyphBottom -> dxblGlyphBottom
  todo 'verify the four positions against the target control at runtime'
end
